        "original_id": "7bbe1548-2ba3-5700-919e-6e1f22bbc056",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Chinese Crested Dog, Chien-gris, Mexican Hairless Dog\n- Concepts: hairless dog breeds, Powderpuff, Hairless, alopecia, canine follicular dysplasia\n\nFacts:\n- The Chien-gris, also called the Gris de Saint-Louis, was a dog breed that originated in Medieval times and is now extinct.\n- The Chinese Crested Dog is a hairless breed of dog.\n- The Chinese Crested Dog has two varieties, Powderpuff and Hairless, and both varieties can be born in the same litter.\n- The Mexican Hairless Dog and the Chinese Crested Dog are among breeds specifically bred for alopecia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ea39fd0a-b21e-5484-84cd-e5be1d92f8fc",
        "text": "Page: Chinese Crested Dog. Sentence: The Chinese crested dog is a hairless breed of dog.\nPage: Chinese Crested Dog. Sentence: Like most hairless dog breeds, the Chinese crested comes in two varieties, with and without fur, which are born in the same litter: the Powderpuff and the Hairless.\nPage: Chien-gris. Sentence: The Chien-gris a.k.a. Gris de Saint-Louis (\"Grey St. Louis Hound\") was a breed of dog, now extinct, which originated in Medieval times.\nPage: Canine follicular dysplasia. Sentence: Certain breeds, such as the Mexican Hairless Dog and Chinese Crested Dog, are bred specifically for alopecia.",
